{
  "id": "public-transit-ridership-service-tra",
  "name": "Transit Ridership and Service Feedback Illustration",
  "description": "Authored, uncalibrated ridership/service feedback illustration. Equations are not verified as a reproduction of Taylor et al. The finite default trajectory is illustrative only, not a forecast or policy assessment. Restricted domain: positive service, nonnegative Car Users, and 0 <= ridership < 1000*service+1 throughout every evaluated state; equality divides by zero and exceeding the threshold reverses the named transfer flows. Initial conditions alone do not ensure this domain remains valid. Parameter exploration can leave it; the runtime does not enforce this restriction. Revenue is a signed cumulative balance; negative balances also reverse the linear service-investment term, without a separate financing model.",
